{"path":"utility/functional/bind12","title":"std::bind1st, std::bind2nd","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>bind1st, <span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>bind2nd","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/functional/bind12","section":"utility","kind":"page","summary":"Binds a given argument x to a first or second parameter of the given binary function object f. That is, stores x within the resulting wrapper, which, if called, passes x as the first or the second parameter of f.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/functional\">&lt;functional&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-until-cxx17\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> F, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/binder12\"><span class=\"kw2737\">std::<span class=\"me2\">binder1st</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>F<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> bind1st<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> F<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> f, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> x <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark\">(deprecated in C++11)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx17\">(removed in C++17)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-until-cxx17\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> F, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/binder12\"><span class=\"kw2738\">std::<span class=\"me2\">binder2nd</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>F<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> bind2nd<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> F<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> f, <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> T<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> x <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark\">(deprecated in C++11)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx17\">(removed in C++17)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Binds a given argument <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x</span></code> to a first or second parameter of the given binary function object <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">f</span></code>. That is, stores <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x</span></code> within the resulting wrapper, which, if called, passes <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x</span></code> as the first or the second parameter of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">f</span></code>.\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Binds the first argument of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">f</span></code> to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x</span></code>. Effectively calls <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/binder12\"><span class=\"kw2737\">std::<span class=\"me2\">binder1st</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>F<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>f, <span class=\"kw1\">typename</span> F<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">first_argument_type</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>x<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Binds the second argument of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">f</span></code> to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x</span></code>. Effectively calls <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/binder12\"><span class=\"kw2738\">std::<span class=\"me2\">binder2nd</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>F<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>f, <span class=\"kw1\">typename</span> F<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">second_argument_type</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>x<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> f\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> pointer to a function to bind an argument to\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> x\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> argument to bind to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">f</span></code>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>A function object wrapping <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">f</span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">x</span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<p>May throw implementation-defined exceptions. \n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;algorithm&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cmath&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cstddef&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;functional&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iomanip&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;vector&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/vector\"><span class=\"kw1277\">std::<span class=\"me2\">vector</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> a <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">0</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">30</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">45</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">60</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">90</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">180</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/vector\"><span class=\"kw1277\">std::<span class=\"me2\">vector</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> r<span class=\"br0\">(</span>a.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> pi <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/acos\"><span class=\"kw1345\">std::<span class=\"me2\">acos</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// since C++20 use std::numbers::pi</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/transform\"><span class=\"kw1601\">std::<span class=\"me2\">transform</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>a.<span class=\"me1\">begin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, a.<span class=\"me1\">end</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, r.<span class=\"me1\">begin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>,\n        std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">bind1st</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/multiplies\"><span class=\"kw1038\">std::<span class=\"me2\">multiplies</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, pi <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <span class=\"nu16\">180.0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"co1\">//  an equivalent lambda is: [pi](double a) { return a * pi / 180.0; });</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw107\">std::<span class=\"me2\">size_t</span></span></a> n <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> n <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> a.<span class=\"me1\">size</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"sy2\">++</span>n<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/manip/setw\"><span class=\"kw1814\">std::<span class=\"me2\">setw</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">3</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> a<span class=\"br0\">[</span>n<span class=\"br0\">]</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"° = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/manip/fixed\"><span class=\"kw1801\">std::<span class=\"me2\">fixed</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> r<span class=\"br0\">[</span>n<span class=\"br0\">]</span>\n                  <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" rad<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/manip/fixed\"><span class=\"kw1804\">std::<span class=\"me2\">defaultfloat</span></span></a><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>\n  0° = 0.000000 rad\n 30° = 0.523599 rad\n 45° = 0.785398 rad\n 60° = 1.047198 rad\n 90° = 1.570796 rad\n180° = 3.141593 rad</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/binder12\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>binder1st</span><span>binder2nd</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-deprecated-cxx11\">(deprecated in C++11)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx17\">(removed in C++17)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  function object holding a binary function and one of its arguments <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/bind_front\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>bind_front</span><span>bind_back</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(C++23)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  bind a variable number of arguments, in order, to a function object <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"utility","title":"Utility library"},{"path":"utility/functional","title":"Function objects"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::bind1st, std::bind2nd","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: until C++17. Binds a given argument x to a first or second parameter of the given binary function object f."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"f, x"},{"label":"Return value","note":"A function object wrapping f and x."},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"May throw implementation-defined exceptions."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"binder1st, binder2nd","note":"function object holding a binary function and one of its arguments"},{"label":"bind_front, bind_back","note":"bind a variable number of arguments, in order, to a function object"}]}]},"standards":["C++11","C++17","C++20","C++23"],"wordCount":296,"codeBlockCount":2}
